# Babysitter Hermes Context

- This repo is standalone. Do not assume it lives inside `optimus_training`.
- Python owns tmux launch, W&B polling, evidence collection, Claude triage, and deterministic gating.
- Hermes owns deep reasoning and subagent delegation only after Claude triage says `needs_action`.
- Preserve the default Hermes model as `anthropic/claude-opus-4-7` unless the user explicitly changes it.
- Do not add OpenAI/OpenRouter requirements to the default setup path.
- Never skip datapoints or silently ignore malformed data. Ask the user what to do.
- Do not mutate training code, configs, data, launch settings, or live training state without explicit user approval.
- Launch training only by wrapping the configured bash script in tmux; do not make Hermes launch jobs.
- Healthy triage sends no message; every non-healthy triage sends or saves a user message.
- Tool handlers should return JSON payloads for both success and failure.
- Write-capable tools must keep outputs inside the configured artifact directory.
- Use `./setup_babysitter_hermes.sh` for fresh machine setup.
- Run `uv run python -m pytest tests -q` after code changes when practical.
